 When there is no such flow,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"findCirculationBarrier(supply:lowerBound:capacity:)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives a set of vertices that proves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Computed by reduction to a maximum flow (push–relabel) from a super source serving each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s imbalance after the lower bounds. Which flow is returned when several exist is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unspecified, but the same input always gives the same result."}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n² √m).","type":"text"}]}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every lower bound is at most its capacity; no value is NaN or infinite; the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"supplies sum to zero; the lower bounds and supplies at a vertex sum without overflow, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"capacity − lower bound does not overflow."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/feasiblecirculation(supply:lowerbound:capacity:)"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/Circulation":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Circulation"}],"url":"\/documentation\/flows\/circulation","role":"symbol","title":"Circulation","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A feasible flow within lower bounds and capacities that meets every supply, returned by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"feasibleCirculation(supply:lowerBound:capacity:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"feasibleCi